    "name": "Small and mid-sized businesses"
   },
   "description": "lumic learns how one job is really done, then builds custom AI for it, such as drafting sales orders from customer emails, entering vendor bills or preparing month-end entries. It works in the systems the team already uses, whether that's an ERP, accounting software, email, spreadsheets or cloud apps, on its own dedicated computer, wherever fits the business. A person approves what it enters, every action is logged, and the team keeps it working for a monthly fee."
  },
  {
   "@type": "FAQPage",
   "@id": "https://get-lumic.com/#faq",
   "mainEntity": [
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "What is an FDE?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "FDE stands for Forward Deployed Engineer. lumic’s FDEs are engineers who come to you, learn how the work is really done, build AI into one job at a time, and keep it working."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Who approves what the agent does?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "A person on your team. The agent makes the entry, and a person checks it and approves it before anything posts. The final post stays in your hands."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "How long does it take to go live?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Weeks, not quarters. After the on-site day, lumic builds and tests the agent in your systems, then it goes live and lumic keeps it working."
     }
    }
   ]
  },
